      "generator": "Codex 内置 ImageGen",
      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story.\nAsset type: six separate original picture-book illustration tiles for an early grade Mandarin lesson about a shadow that accompanies you. Generate a single flat atlas with exactly 3 columns × 2 rows of equal square tiles. Each cell is full-bleed and self-contained. Grid boundaries at exactly one-third, two-thirds width and one-half height. Keep every subject at least 10% away from its cell edges. No visible seams needed but use distinct simple backgrounds per cell for cropping. No words, numbers, letters, borders or watermark anywhere. No shared objects crossing any cell edge.\nStyle: fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut-paper contours, deep pine green and warm cream, apricot and persimmon-orange accents. Light, restrained backgrounds. Simple large shapes so what happened is recognizable in a thumbnail, child-friendly without caricature. Keep the same main kid in the top three panels: cropped short dark hair, orange scarf, sea-green jacket, plain dark shorts, warm childlike face.\nTop left: at a courtyard entrance on a sunny day, this child pauses mid-step on a pale flat path. Clearly show the entire child head to both shoes and the dark coherent silhouette on the ground attached to their feet in front-right of the child. Show quiet warm plaster walls and a small deep-green open gate.\nTop middle: the same child gently bends a little to greet one small clearly black pet dog in profile. Show the four-legged dog and the child's fully visible legs, simple courtyard backdrop.\nTop right: the same child and a peer walk together on a pale path, same travel direction, expressive but relaxed, one shadow attached to each pair of feet, modest distance between the figures.\nBottom left: a NEW distinct pair of children, a kid with an apricot cap and a kid with a green backpack, walking in profile SIDE BY SIDE toward the RIGHT on a quiet cream garden path, both faces oriented right. Both full bodies are near each other and both in motion, no other people.\nBottom middle: same two new kids on a similar path, separated from one another, one visibly facing and walking LEFT and one visibly facing and walking RIGHT. Show an obvious gap between them and different directions. Both full bodies, no other people.\nBottom right: only two inanimate objects placed separately on one plain small bench, one orange cap and one neatly folded green umbrella, zero people, cream ground and muted green trees.\nConstraints: Use original compositions and character designs. Prioritize unmistakable shadow attachment or travel directions. Do not introduce extra props that compete with the subjects. Avoid photorealism, 3D, character overlap, complicated cast shadows, text or incidental symbols."
    },
